  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: The only image-only result so far (config_010, resnet50 singleprofile) is very weak at 0.208 accuracy, while RNA-only models range from 0.48 to 0.65. We have no data on whether a stronger pretrained image encoder (ImageNet ViT-L) provides any meaningful signal for this task. 2) What this tests: config_013 isolates the effect of image encoder quality (ViT-L vs. ResNet50) in the simplest possible setting (singleprofile, image-only), directly answering whether the image modality carries useful discriminative information at all. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: This single-variable test gates an entire branch of the search space. If ViT-L singleprofile remains very weak (<0.30), we can confidently deprioritize all 36 multimodal configurations and redirect limited budget toward refining the RNA pipeline (e.g., confirming scvi_n200 multiprofile as the best RNA setup, or testing scgpt+transformer). If ViT-L shows substantially better performance, multimodal fusion with scvi_n200 becomes a high-value direction. Under a tight budget, this experiment maximizes information gain by resolving the most consequential open question—whether the image modality is worth integrating at all—before committing to any multimodal configuration."
